 bind and activate SMAD transcriptional regulators, SMAD2 and SMAD3. Receptor for activin AB, activin B, activin E and NODAL. Upon NODAL binding, activation results in increased apoptosis and reduced proliferation through suppression of AKT signaling and the activation of Smad2-dependent signaling pathway in pancreatic beta-cells, trophoblasts, epithelial or neuronal cells (PubMed:15531507, PubMed:15150278). Acts as a positive regulator for macrophage activation partially through down-regulation of PPARG expression (By similarity)"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "L-threonyl-[receptor-protein] + ATP = O-phospho-L-threonyl-[receptor-protein] + ADP + H(+)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:44880"}, {"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA-COMP:11024"}, {"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA-COMP:11025"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:15378"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:30013"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:30616"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:61977"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:456216"}], "ecNumber": "2.7.11.30"}}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "L-seryl-[receptor-protein] + ATP = O-phospho-L-seryl-[receptor-protein] + ADP + H(+)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:18673"}, {"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA-COMP:11022"}, {"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA-COMP:11023"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:15378"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:29999"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:30616"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:83421"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:456216"}], "ecNumber": "2.7.11.30"}}, {"commentType": "COFACTOR", "cofactors": [{"name": "Mg(2+)", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "cofactorCrossReference": {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:18420"}}, {"name": "Mn(2+)", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000305"}], "cofactorCrossReference": {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHE